Begin Exploring Related Columns
Relevant columns and their potential usage for the requested report  
• olist_orders.order_id : identifier that will be counted.  
• olist_orders.order_status : filter to keep only rows whose value is 'delivered'.  
• olist_orders.order_delivered_customer_date : contains the UTC‑like time‑stamp of the real delivery; we can take   
 • Year → substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4)  
 • Month→ substr(order_delivered_customer_date,6,2)  
Conditions that will be useful  
1. olist_orders.order_status = 'delivered'  
2. substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')  
3. order_delivered_customer_date IS NOT NULL (safety)  

Below are ten exploratory SQL queries (all different) that gradually surface the pieces needed for the final crosstab report.  
Every query is written with a short description, uses DISTINCT whenever practical, and is limited to 20 rows to remain lightweight.

```sql
-- 1) Description: See all distinct order_status values so we know the exact spelling to filter.
SELECT DISTINCT "order_status"
FROM "olist_orders"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: Inspect the raw delivery time‑stamps (distinct values, truncated to 20).
SELECT DISTINCT "order_delivered_customer_date"
FROM "olist_orders"
WHERE "order_delivered_customer_date" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: List distinct years extracted from the delivery date.
SELECT DISTINCT substr("order_delivered_customer_date",1,4) AS "year"
FROM "olist_orders"
WHERE "order_delivered_customer_date" IS NOT NULL
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: List distinct months (01‑12) extracted from the delivery date, ordered.
SELECT DISTINCT substr("order_delivered_customer_date",6,2) AS "month"
FROM "olist_orders"
WHERE "order_delivered_customer_date" IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY "month"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Get distinct year‑month combinations for *delivered* orders only.
SELECT DISTINCT
       substr("order_delivered_customer_date",1,4) AS "year",
       substr("order_delivered_customer_date",6,2) AS "month"
FROM "olist_orders"
WHERE "order_status" = 'delivered'
  AND "order_delivered_customer_date" IS NOT NULL
ORDER BY "year","month"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Count delivered orders per year‑month (all years).
SELECT
  substr("order_delivered_customer_date",1,4) AS "year",
  substr("order_delivered_customer_date",6,2) AS "month",
  COUNT("order_id")                              AS "delivered_orders"
FROM "olist_orders"
WHERE "order_status" = 'delivered'
  AND "order_delivered_customer_date" IS NOT NULL
GROUP BY "year","month"
ORDER BY "year","month"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Same as #6 but restricted to 2016‑2018.
SELECT
  substr("order_delivered_customer_date",1,4) AS "year",
  substr("order_delivered_customer_date",6,2) AS "month",
  COUNT("order_id")                              AS "delivered_orders"
FROM "olist_orders"
WHERE "order_status" = 'delivered'
  AND substr("order_delivered_customer_date",1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')
GROUP BY "year","month"
ORDER BY "year","month"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Aggregate by month only (Jan‑Dec) summing delivered orders for each of the three years together.
SELECT
  substr("order_delivered_customer_date",6,2)     AS "month",
  COUNT("order_id")                               AS "delivered_orders_2016_2018"
FROM "olist_orders"
WHERE "order_status" = 'delivered'
  AND substr("order_delivered_customer_date",1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')
GROUP BY "month"
ORDER BY "month"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Produce a narrow table with conditional aggregation—counts per year in separate columns.
SELECT
  substr("order_delivered_customer_date",6,2) AS "month",
  SUM(CASE WHEN substr("order_delivered_customer_date",1,4)='2016' THEN 1 END) AS "y2016",
  SUM(CASE WHEN substr("order_delivered_customer_date",1,4)='2017' THEN 1 END) AS "y2017",
  SUM(CASE WHEN substr("order_delivered_customer_date",1,4)='2018' THEN 1 END) AS "y2018"
FROM "olist_orders"
WHERE "order_status" = 'delivered'
  AND substr("order_delivered_customer_date",1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')
GROUP BY "month"
ORDER BY "month"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: Same as #9 but without LIMIT so it is ready as the final requested report.
SELECT
  substr("order_delivered_customer_date",6,2) AS "month",
  SUM(CASE WHEN substr("order_delivered_customer_date",1,4)='2016' THEN 1 END) AS "delivered_2016",
  SUM(CASE WHEN substr("order_delivered_customer_date",1,4)='2017' THEN 1 END) AS "delivered_2017",
  SUM(CASE WHEN substr("order_delivered_customer_date",1,4)='2018' THEN 1 END) AS "delivered_2018"
FROM "olist_orders"
WHERE "order_status" = 'delivered'
  AND substr("order_delivered_customer_date",1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')
GROUP BY "month"
ORDER BY "month";
```
